\section{Gauge-orbit consistency fixes the quadratic term}

The inconsistency of \cref{eq:p3-linear-try} can now be diagnosed directly under a change of representative. The free current transforms as
\begin{align}
J_{(0)}^{\prime\mu}
&=\ii q\left[
\Phi'^*\partial^\mu\Phi'-(\partial^\mu\Phi'^*)\Phi'
\right]\\
&=J_{(0)}^\mu+2q^2|\Phi|^2\partial^\mu\alpha.
\label{eq:p3-free-current-local-transform}
\end{align}
Consequently,
\begin{align}
\delta(-A_\mu J_{(0)}^\mu)
&=-(\partial_\mu\alpha)J_{(0)}^\mu
-A_\mu\delta J_{(0)}^\mu\\
&=-(\partial_\mu\alpha)J_{(0)}^\mu
-2q^2A_\mu|\Phi|^2\partial^\mu\alpha.
\end{align}
The first term cancels \cref{eq:p3-local-L-variation}; the second is the local remainder. Its tensor structure is not arbitrary. To first order in \(\alpha\),
\begin{equation}
\delta\!\left(q^2A_\mu A^\mu|\Phi|^2\right)
=2q^2A_\mu|\Phi|^2\partial^\mu\alpha.
\label{eq:p3-seagull-local-repair}
\end{equation}
The quadratic interaction inferred from representative independence is exactly the term whose variation with respect to \(A_\mu\) supplies the source correction anticipated in \cref{eq:p3-interacting-current-preview}. Rather than add further terms order by order, the local comparison law can be repaired directly.

\section{Constructing the covariant derivative}

We want a derivative-like object whose result transforms with the same local phase as the field:
\begin{equation}
(D_\mu\Phi)'=\ee^{-\ii q\alpha}D_\mu\Phi.
\label{eq:p3-covariance-target}
\end{equation}
The Maxwell orbit is already fixed:
\[
A_\mu'=A_\mu+\partial_\mu\alpha.
\]
Try
\begin{equation}
\boxed{D_\mu\equiv\partial_\mu+\ii qA_\mu.}
\label{eq:p3-covariant-derivative}
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{align}
D_\mu'\Phi'
&=\left[\partial_\mu+\ii q(A_\mu+\partial_\mu\alpha)\right]
\ee^{-\ii q\alpha}\Phi\\
&=\ee^{-\ii q\alpha}
\left[\partial_\mu\Phi-\ii q(\partial_\mu\alpha)\Phi
+\ii qA_\mu\Phi+\ii q(\partial_\mu\alpha)\Phi\right]\\
&=\ee^{-\ii q\alpha}D_\mu\Phi.
\label{eq:p3-D-covariance-check}
\end{align}
The derivative mismatch is cancelled point by point. The Maxwell potential, redundant as a choice of representative, now serves as the connection that compares charged phases locally.

The commutator of two such comparisons returns the electromagnetic field strength:
\begin{align}
[D_\mu,D_\nu]\Phi
&=\ii q(\partial_\mu A_\nu-\partial_\nu A_\mu)\Phi\\
&=\boxed{\ii qF_{\mu\nu}\Phi.}
\label{eq:p3-D-commutator}
\end{align}
Thus the local curvature of the phase-comparison rule is the gauge-invariant field already measured by \(\Efield\) and \(\Bfield\).

\section{The coupled action and the seagull term}

The lowest-derivative completion of the free scalar kinetic term is now
\begin{equation}
\boxed{
\Lagr_{\rm SQED}
=-\frac14F_{\mu\nu}F^{\mu\nu}
+(D_\mu\Phi)^*D^\mu\Phi-m^2|\Phi|^2.}
\label{eq:p3-SQED-L}
\end{equation}
This is the minimal electromagnetic model needed here, not the most general renormalizable scalar theory. A separately gauge-invariant scalar self-interaction \(-\lambda_\Phi(\Phi^*\Phi)^2\) is allowed and is in general required once scalar QED is treated as a renormalized quantum theory. We set \(\lambda_\Phi=0\) in this Part because it does 